<section id="research-partnerships" class="bhd-page__cards-section bhd-partnership-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Research partnerships</p>
  <h2>Relevant questions, appropriate methods, transparent results</h2>
  <p>Research should answer useful questions and make future product or health claims more precise.</p>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
    <article><h3>Relevant questions</h3><p>Study problems that matter outside the lab.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Appropriate methods</h3><p>Match study design to the claim being tested.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Transparent results</h3><p>Publish and distinguish findings from interpretation.</p></article>
  </div>
  <p>Best Hydrate’s research program is growing; completed work and future questions are kept separate.</p>
  <a class="bhd-page__text-link" href="/pages/research-publications">Research &amp; Impact →</a>
</section>

<section id="retail-distribution" class="bhd-page__cards-section bhd-partnership-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Retail &amp; distribution</p>
  <h2>Demand, reliable supply and measured rollout</h2>
  <p>Retail expansion should follow customer demand, reliable supply and a clear reason for the product to be on shelf.</p>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
    <article><h3>Product fit</h3><p>A differentiated hydration product with simple positioning.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Reliable supply</h3><p>Growth should not outrun fulfillment.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Measured rollout</h3><p>Learn from each channel before adding complexity.</p></article>
  </div>
  <p>Best Hydrate currently sells online while building broader distribution.</p>
  <a class="bhd-page__text-link" href="/products/lemonade-best-hydrate">View Product →</a>
</section>

<section id="community-humanitarian" class="bhd-page__cards-section bhd-partnership-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Community &amp; humanitarian</p>
  <h2>Context, local partners and evidence come first</h2>
  <p>Hydration access matters most where safe water, supply chains and health resources are constrained.</p>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
    <article><h3>Context first</h3><p>A product is only useful when it fits local needs and infrastructure.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Partners matter</h3><p>Work through organizations that understand the setting.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Evidence matters</h3><p>Humanitarian intent does not substitute for appropriate validation.</p></article>
  </div>
  <p>Best Hydrate is exploring this area carefully; it is not presented as a deployed humanitarian solution.</p>
  <a class="bhd-page__text-link" href="/pages/eco-humanitarian">Humanitarian Hydration →</a>
</section>

<section id="athlete-team-event" class="bhd-page__cards-section bhd-partnership-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Athlete, team &amp; event partnerships</p>
  <h2>Performance relationships belong in a real use context</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
    <article><h3>Athletes</h3><p>Training, competition, travel and recovery create real hydration decisions. Athlete collaborations should show that context without promising that a product caused a result.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Teams &amp; coaches</h3><p>Education, routines and team environments can make hydration collaboration useful when roles and claims are clear.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Events</h3><p>Sampling and event support can introduce the product in context without turning participation into scientific endorsement.</p></article>
  </div>
  <a class="bhd-page__text-link" href="/pages/athletes-ambassadors">Athletics &amp; Ambassadors →</a>
</section>

